<https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24305436> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-17"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24305436> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3246-3531> .
<https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24305436> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Idealised reconstruction of a stepped LEGO pyramid with four grey stair arms (seven levels) and a small temple with four corner pillars on top, a hobby build by Daria Stefan (TU Wien), rebuilt procedurally from clean LEGO bricks after a KIRI Engine scan. Only dimensions and structure were read from the scan; no scan mesh or texture was reused. AI disclosure: the reconstruction was generated with Claude (Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5) on behalf of Florian Thiery. It is an interpretation model, not a measurement." .
<https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24305436> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> "10.5281/zenodo.24310030" .
<https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24305436> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026-11-17"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24305436> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> .
<https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24305436> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html> .
<https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24305436> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/provenance> "{\"ai_involvement\": \"Generated with Claude (Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5), session 2026-11-12 to 2026-11-17\", \"alignment\": \"Scan rotated by 16.25 degrees (sharpness histogram around the temple centre); grid and brick height derived from 4 million surface points (about 13 cells per stud)\", \"assumptions\": \"Seven levels after photo and builder statement (the scan suggests up to eight, the lowest probably merged with the table); pillar rotations 14, -12, 16, -9 degrees and block twist estimated by eye; stair arms on levels 6/7 symmetric in the model but not fully in the photo; scan ground plane not carried over\", \"bricks\": \"white 32x 2x4, 20x 2x2, 12x 1x1, 8 special 1x2/1x4; grey 70x 2x4, 9x 2x2\", \"colours_rgb\": \"white (245, 245, 241), grey (48, 50, 48)\", \"method\": \"Procedural rebuild from idealised bricks (script build_m3.py, version 4), not a cleaned scan mesh\", \"random_seed\": \"numpy.random.default_rng(5)\", \"reproducibility\": \"Re-running the script reproduces lego3.glb byte-identically with Python 3.13.18, numpy 2.5.3, trimesh 5.2.1, Pillow 12.3.0, scipy 1.18.1 (sha256 543a744f2ec29f9b65c12008cd01b3b2fe829ccf1eeef1bc74b40a27943eac8b)\", \"structure\": \"7 levels; four stair arms 4 studs wide reaching 9, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3 studs from the centre; white corner areas 6x6 down to 2x2; temple of 4 layers with four white 1x1 corner pillars\"}" .
